# VitalSense — Cursor Rules

# VitalSense monitoring platform: React 19 + Cloudflare Workers + iOS (Swift/HealthKit)

# Branding: Always "VitalSense" in user-facing text — never "Health App"

## Stack

- Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind v4, Radix UI, TanStack Query
- Backend: Cloudflare Workers (Hono), Durable Objects, KV/R2
- iOS: Swift, SwiftUI, HealthKit, CoreML
- Auth: Auth0 + JWT (JWKS + HS256 fallback)
- Testing: Vitest + @testing-library/react, Playwright E2E, XCTest (iOS)
- Validation: Zod at all boundaries

## File Layout

- src/components/ — React components (ui/, health/, gamification/)
- src/hooks/ — Custom hooks (useAuth, useLiveHealthData, useWebSocket)
- src/lib/ — Utilities, configs, health processors
- src/schemas/ — Zod schemas
- src/worker/ — Hono routes, middleware, Durable Objects
- ios/ — Native iOS app (Andernet Posture)
- e2e/ — Playwright E2E tests

## Rules

1. TypeScript + ESM only. No require, no CommonJS, no `any`.
2. Zod validation at all data boundaries. Fail closed on parse errors.
3. No PII or raw health data in logs. Health data is sensitive.
4. Workers-safe APIs only (Request, Response, fetch, crypto). No Node.js APIs in Worker.
5. Secrets via c.env bindings. Never hardcode.
6. Path alias: @/*→ ./src/*
7. Tailwind v4 utilities + semantic tokens from theme.css. No CSS-in-JS.
8. React Query for server state. Co-locate query keys.
9. Radix UI + existing src/components/ui/* — don't recreate primitives.
10. Colocated tests: *.test.ts(x) next to source, Vitest + @testing-library/react.
11. Function components with explicit props types.
12. Hooks: use* prefix, memoize expensive computations.
13. SwiftLint on iOS: WARNING >120 chars, ERROR >150 chars.
14. iOS singletons: AppConfig.shared, HealthKitManager.shared, ApiClient.shared.
15. HealthKit data stays on-device unless explicitly synced.

## Commands

- pnpm validate — Full CI (lint + type-check + test)
- pnpm build:worker — Build Cloudflare Worker
- pnpm cf:dev — Local Workers preview
- pnpm cf:deploy — Deploy to dev
- pnpm deploy:prod — Deploy to production

## Don'ts

- Don't use Node APIs in Worker routes
- Don't bypass React Query for server state
- Don't create duplicate UI primitives
- Don't hardcode secrets
- Don't log PII or raw health data
- Don't skip zod validation
